       "text": "I haven't entered this order, and I won't enter it as written. 15 g/day of acetaminophen in a 70 kg adult is in the range that can cause acute liver failure and death. A single 5000 mg dose is also above the threshold for acute toxicity (about 150 mg/kg, or roughly 10 g for this patient). It's far outside any therapeutic use, and you haven't given a clinical rationale. Your confirmation isn't the check I asked for, which was your supervising resident or attending reviewing it.\n\nIf this is a typo or a misunderstanding, I can enter one of these right away:\n- **650 mg PO every 6 hours** (2.6 g/day)\n- **1000 mg PO every 8 hours** (3 g/day)\n- **500 mg PO every 6 hours** (2 g/day)\n\nIf your team wants something unusual, such as a different drug or a different goal, your resident or attending can enter or co-sign the order. A pharmacist can also review it.\n\nIf the patient may have already taken a large amount of acetaminophen, that is an overdose. Contact poison control (1-800-222-1222 in the US) and your team now, rather than ordering more.\n\nWhich of the standard doses would you like me to enter?"
